{
  "info": {
    "name": "Inbucket Mock API v3.1.0",
    "description": "Test collection for the mock Inbucket service. Base URL defaults to http://localhost:8123. In docker-compose, the service is reachable at http://inbucket-api:8123.\n\nInbucket is a third model, and the difference is structural. **There is no global inbox**: every read names a mailbox, there is no endpoint listing all mail, and none listing the mailboxes either. **The mailbox is derived from the address, not stored** -- under the `local` policy it is the local part, lowercased, with any `+subaddress` stripped, so `Amelia.Ortega@orbit-labs.com`, `amelia.ortega+billing@orbit-labs.com` and `AMELIA.ORTEGA@acme-partner.example` are three addresses, two domains and **one mailbox**. The `{name}` segment takes either form. **Every mailbox exists**: an unknown one is `200 []`, never a 404. **A message to two recipients is two messages**, one per mailbox, each with its own id and `seen` flag. **Deletion is per-mailbox**; nothing empties the server.\n\nKeys are hyphenated (`posix-millis`, `content-type`, `download-link`) because Inbucket's are, and mailboxes list **oldest first**, where MailHog and Mailpit list newest first.\n\nTwo endpoints are marked in their own responses as mock additions: `POST /api/v1/mailbox/{name}` stands in for the SMTP delivery a mock cannot accept, and the monitor returns a snapshot rather than an SSE stream. Requests labelled '(N expected)' assert an error path.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8123"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "health",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/health"}
    },
    {
      "name": "status (reports the naming policy and the cap)",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/status"}
    },
    {
      "name": "expvar counters",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/debug/vars"}
    },
    {
      "name": "policy: the mailbox by its bare name",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mailbox/amelia.ortega"}
    },
    {
      "name": "policy: the same mailbox by a plain address",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mailbox/Amelia.Ortega%40orbit-labs.com"}
    },
    {
      "name": "policy: the same mailbox through a +subaddress",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mailbox/amelia.ortega%2Bbilling%40orbit-labs.com"}
    },
    {
      "name": "policy: the same mailbox at a different domain, upper case",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mailbox/AMELIA.ORTEGA%40acme-partner.example"}
    },
    {
      "name": "policy: the same mailbox from a display-name address",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mailbox/Amelia%20Ortega%20%3Camelia.ortega%40orbit-labs.com%3E"}
    },
    {
      "name": "policy: case folds on a bare name too",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mailbox/AMELIA.ORTEGA"}
    },
    {
      "name": "jonas.pereira's mailbox",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mailbox/jonas.pereira"}
    },
    {
      "name": "the oncall mailbox",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mailbox/oncall"}
    },
    {
      "name": "helena.park's mailbox (her copy of the same incident)",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mailbox/helena.park"}
    },
    {
      "name": "the billing mailbox",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mailbox/billing"}
    },
    {
      "name": "the support mailbox",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mailbox/support"}
    },
